<report>
<title>Fully nested/hierarchical random analysis of variance</title>

<p>Variables:@tlist</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Source of Variation</th><th>Sum Squares</th><th>DF</th><th>Mean Square</th></tr>
<tr><td>Between Groups</td><td>@{grp_sum:roundu}</td><td>@grp_df</td><td>@{grp_mean:roundu}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Between Subgroups within Groups</td><td>@{sub_sum:roundu}</td><td>@sub_df</td><td>@{sub_mean:roundu}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Residual</td><td>@{res_sum:roundu}</td><td>@res_df</td><td>@{res_mean:roundu}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Total</td><td>@{tot_sum:roundu}</td><td>@tot_df</td><td></td></tr>
</table>

<p>F (VR between groups) = @{f_1:roundu}  <pval>@{p_1:pval}</pval></p>

<p>F (using group/subgroup msqr) = @{f_2:roundu}  <pval>@{p_2:pval}</pval></p>

<p>F (VR between subgroups within groups) = @{f_3:roundu}  <pval>@{p_3:pval}</pval></p>
</report>
